{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-romans-011",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 11,
  "title": "Romans 11",
  "display_title": "Romans 11",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "romans",
  "book": "Romans",
  "bookName": "Romans",
  "bookOrder": 45,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 11,
  "sortOrder": 45011,
  "verseCount": 36,
  "aliases": [
    "Rom",
    "Ro",
    "Rm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "I say then, Hath God cast away his people? God forbid. For I also am an Israelite, of the seed of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "God hath not cast away his people which he foreknew. Wot ye not what the scripture saith of Elias? how he maketh intercession to God against Israel, saying,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Lord, they have killed thy prophets, and digged down thine altars; and I am left alone, and they seek my life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "But what saith the answer of God unto him? I have reserved to myself seven thousand men, who have not bowed the knee to the image of Baal.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Even so then at this present time also there is a remnant according to the election of grace.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And if by grace, then is it no more of works: otherwise grace is no more grace. But if it be of works, then is it no more grace: otherwise work is no more work.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "What then? Israel hath not obtained that which he seeketh for; but the election hath obtained it, and the rest were blinded.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "(According as it is written, God hath given them the spirit of slumber, eyes that they should not see, and ears that they should not hear;) unto this day.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "And David saith, Let their table be made a snare, and a trap, and a stumblingblock, and a recompence unto them:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Let their eyes be darkened, that they may not see, and bow down their back alway.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "I say then, Have they stumbled that they should fall? God forbid: but rather through their fall salvation is come unto the Gentiles, for to provoke them to jealousy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Now if the fall of them be the riches of the world, and the diminishing of them the riches of the Gentiles; how much more their fulness?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "For I speak to you Gentiles, inasmuch as I am the apostle of the Gentiles, I magnify mine office:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "If by any means I may provoke to emulation them which are my flesh, and might save some of them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "For if the casting away of them be the reconciling of the world, what shall the receiving of them be, but life from the dead?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "For if the firstfruit be holy, the lump is also holy: and if the root be holy, so are the branches.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And if some of the branches be broken off, and thou, being a wild olive tree, wert graffed in among them, and with them partakest of the root and fatness of the olive tree;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Boast not against the branches. But if thou boast, thou bearest not the root, but the root thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Thou wilt say then, The branches were broken off, that I might be graffed in.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Well; because of unbelief they were broken off, and thou standest by faith. Be not highminded, but fear:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "For if God spared not the natural branches, take heed lest he also spare not thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Behold therefore the goodness and severity of God: on them which fell, severity; but toward thee, goodness, if thou continue in his goodness: otherwise thou also shalt be cut off.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "And they also, if they abide not still in unbelief, shall be graffed in: for God is able to graff them in again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "For if thou wert cut out of the olive tree which is wild by nature, and wert graffed contrary to nature into a good olive tree: how much more shall these, which be the natural branches, be graffed into their own olive tree?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "For I would not, brethren, that ye should be ignorant of this mystery, lest ye should be wise in your own conceits; that blindness in part is happened to Israel, until the fulness of the Gentiles be come in.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "And so all Israel shall be saved: as it is written, There shall come out of Sion the Deliverer, and shall turn away ungodliness from Jacob:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "For this is my covenant unto them, when I shall take away their sins.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "As concerning the gospel, they are enemies for your sakes: but as touching the election, they are beloved for the fathers’ sakes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "For the gifts and calling of God are without repentance.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "For as ye in times past have not believed God, yet have now obtained mercy through their unbelief:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Even so have these also now not believed, that through your mercy they also may obtain mercy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "For God hath concluded them all in unbelief, that he might have mercy upon all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "O the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and knowledge of God! how unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past finding out!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "For who hath known the mind of the Lord? or who hath been his counsellor?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "Or who hath first given to him, and it shall be recompensed unto him again?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:romans:11:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "For of him, and through him, and to him, are all things: to whom be glory for ever. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Romans 11:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:romans:11:36"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
